<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michael Obrenović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1823–1868</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mihailo Obrenović III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michael Obrenović (Mihailo Obrenović III) was prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1839 to 1842 and again from 1860 until his assassination in 1868. In his second reign he modernised the army and administration and worked for a Balkan alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. His diplomacy secured the withdrawal of the last Ottoman garrisons from Serbian fortresses, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, in 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/michael-obrenovic.jpg" alt="Michael Obrenović" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Böss · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mihailo_Obrenovi%C4%87_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
